{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794348754,"nonce":"hOuEs2p5DRwQadp+rrxSALrkGNk=","message":"First LLVM-vs-direct measurements, Mac (M-series, 10 cores), commit aee2fa43, ASH_WASM_DIRECT=1 vs unset, target wasm32-wasip1-threads, `--no-air-cache`. NOT trusted as final: the machine's 1-minute load was 15 to 39 throughout (other sessions), each build and cold launch ran once, and the standing rule says the NUC confirms perf. CPU time (user+sys) is the steadier column.\n\nLarge program, unit.hl (8688 functions, 76.6% direct):\n- build wall / CPU: LLVM 78.3 s / 145 s, direct 47.0 s / 83 s (-40% / -43%). With fibers: 50.7 s / 125 s vs 31.3 s / 77 s (-38% / -38%).\n- module size: 20.5 MB vs 16.4 MB (-20%). With fibers: 28.3 MB vs 24.9 MB (-12%).\n- cold launch (wasmtime compile + `--ash-list`), wall / CPU: 3.63 s / 11.2 s vs 2.07 s / 9.3 s (-43% / -18%). With fibers: 10.2 s / 36.0 s vs 9.4 s / 37.2 s (-8% / +3%): no gain.\n- warm launch (compile cached): 0.33 to 0.39 s vs 0.21 s. With fibers: 0.40 s vs 0.45 to 0.48 s (slightly worse; inside the noise at this load).\n\nSmall programs (hello, bench): build 0.3 to 0.7 s either way, warm launch 0.09 to 0.10 s either way. No difference.\n\nSteady state, TestWasmBench in-program timings (ms), LLVM vs direct:\n- fib 175 to 183 vs 80 to 84. With fibers 173 to 181 vs 82 to 86.\n- loopSum 550 vs 553. With fibers 429 to 438 vs 562 to 568 (direct 30% slower).\n- grid 195 vs 205. With fibers 200 to 206 vs 209 to 211 (about 5% slower).\n\nReading: direct cuts build time and module size for a large program and speeds up call-heavy code, but the cold launch of a fiber-transformed module costs about 36 CPU-s here whichever backend made it, so the fibers module's compile cost, not the backend, now dominates launch. Direct code is slower than LLVM on a tight arithmetic loop under fibers (cause not yet looked at).","files":null}]}